<title>CANADA: Government of Canada sells no gold in December.</title>
<headline>Government of Canada sells no gold in December.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada did not sell any gold in December, leaving reserves at 3.1 million ounces as of December 31, the Finance Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Canadian government has a policy of gradually selling off its gold reserves and replacing them with interest-bearing assets, but the department's foreign reserves statement showed nil for the category &quot;gain on gold sales&quot; in December.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
